.TH DAGonFS 1 "21 June 2026" "DAGonFS" "DAGonFS"
.SH NAME
DAGonFS \- MPI-distributed in-memory filesystem using FUSE3
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B DAGonFS_Launcher
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B DAGonFS
is an in-memory FUSE3 filesystem for temporary workflow data. It coordinates file
data between MPI processes using either a client-server or peer-to-peer model.
It is not durable storage: unmounting or stopping the service discards its contents.
.PP
.B DAGonFS_Launcher
reads DAGonFS.ini in its current directory and invokes MPI with the configured model,
mountpoint, and logging settings. The executable requires FUSE3 and Open MPI.
.SH POSIX OPERATIONS
The filesystem supports regular file and directory creation, lookup, reads, writes,
renames, links, symbolic links, metadata changes, extended attributes, statfs, and
the FUSE lifecycle operations. It reports no retained byte-range locks for getlk.
Extensions such as fallocate, ioctl, polling, and retained byte-range locks are not
provided.
.SH ADDITIONAL INFORMATION
Project documentation is available in the repository's docs directory.
